# 低频词汇 List07
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List07核心词汇

{{default}}{/dɪˈfɔːlt/}{默认；违约}{The system uses the default settings unless changed.}}
{{deficiency}}{/dɪˈfɪʃnsi/}{缺乏；不足}{A deficiency in vitamin C can cause health problems.}}
{{deficit}}{/ˈdefɪsɪt/}{赤字；亏损}{The trade deficit widened to a record high.}}
{{defy}}{/dɪˈfaɪ/}{违抗；蔑视}{The protesters defied the government's ban on gatherings.}}
{{delegate}}{/ˈdelɪɡeɪt/}{委托；代表}{Effective leaders know when to delegate responsibilities.}}
{{demographic}}{/ˌdeməˈɡræfɪk/}{人口统计的}{The demographic profile of the region has shifted considerably.}}
{{denounce}}{/dɪˈnaʊns/}{谴责；告发}{Human rights groups denounced the use of torture.}}
{{dense}}{/dens/}{密集的；浓密的}{The city center has a dense concentration of skyscrapers.}}
{{deploy}}{/dɪˈplɔɪ/}{部署；使用}{The company deployed additional resources to meet demand.}}
{{depression}}{/dɪˈpreʃn/}{沮丧；萧条}{Economic depression led to widespread unemployment.}}
{{descend}}{/dɪˈsend/}{下降；遗传}{The temperature descended below freezing overnight.}}
{{designate}}{/ˈdezɪɡneɪt/}{指定；命名}{The building was designated as a historic landmark.}}
{{despair}}{/dɪˈspeər/}{绝望；失望}{The community refused to give in to despair.}}
{{destiny}}{/ˈdestɪni/}{命运；天命}{She believed she was destined for greatness.}}
{{detach}}{/dɪˈtætʃ/}{分离；拆开}{The label can be easily detached from the package.}}
{{detain}}{/dɪˈteɪn/}{拘留；扣留}{Security detained the man for further questioning.}}
{{deteriorate}}{/dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt/}{恶化；退化}{Relations between the two countries continued to deteriorate.}}
{{devastate}}{/ˈdevəsteɪt/}{毁灭；摧毁}{The earthquake devastated entire villages.}}
{{devise}}{/dɪˈvaɪz/}{设计；发明}{The team devised a creative solution to the problem.}}
{{diagnose}}{/ˈdaɪəɡnəʊz/}{诊断；判断}{The doctor diagnosed the illness at an early stage.}}
{{differ}}{/ˈdɪfər/}{不同；意见不合}{Opinions differ on the best approach to the problem.}}
{{digest}}{/daɪˈdʒest/}{消化；理解}{The report contains a lot of data that takes time to digest.}}
{{dilemma}}{/dɪˈlemə/}{困境；进退两难}{The company faced a dilemma between cost and quality.}}
{{dimension}}{/daɪˈmenʃn/}{维度；方面}{The problem has a political dimension that cannot be ignored.}}
{{diplomacy}}{/dɪˈpləʊməsi/}{外交；交际手段}{Diplomacy is preferred over military action in resolving disputes.}}
{{discern}}{/dɪˈsɜːn/}{辨别；觉察}{It was difficult to discern the truth from the conflicting reports.}}
{{disclose}}{/dɪsˈkləʊz/}{揭露；公开}{The company failed to disclose the risks to investors.}}
{{discrete}}{/dɪˈskriːt/}{离散的；不连续的}{The data was divided into discrete categories for analysis.}}
{{discretion}}{/dɪˈskreʃn/}{谨慎；自行决定权}{Employees are expected to exercise discretion in such matters.}}
{{disguise}}{/dɪsˈɡaɪz/}{伪装；掩饰}{The plan was a disguised attempt to cut costs.}}
